{"id":"ziph","name":"Ziph","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:ziph"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Ziph","text":"Flowing. (1.) A son of Jehaleleel (1 Chr. 4:16). (2.) A city in the south of Judah (Josh. 15:24), probably at the pass of Sufah. (3.) A city in the mountains of Judah (Josh. 15:55), identified with the uninhabited ruins of Tell ez-Zif, about 5 miles south-east of Hebron. Here David hid himself during his wanderings (1 Sam. 23:19; Ps. 54, title)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2128","lemma":"זִיף","xlit":"Zîyph","gloss":"Ziph, the name of a place in Palestine","kjv":"Ziph","count":9,"share":1},{"strong":"H4057","lemma":"מִדְבָּר","xlit":"midbâr","gloss":"a pasture","kjv":"desert, south, speech, wilderness","count":4,"share":0.44},{"strong":"H7586","lemma":"שָׁאוּל","xlit":"Shâʼûwl","gloss":"Shaul, the name of an Edomite and two Israelites","kjv":"Saul, Shaul","count":4,"share":0.44},{"strong":"H4584","lemma":"מָעוֹן","xlit":"Mâʻôwn","gloss":"Maon, the name of an Israelite and of a place in Palesti","kjv":"Maon, Maonites","count":2,"share":0.22},{"strong":"H4762","lemma":"מַרְאֵשָׁה","xlit":"Marʼêshâh","gloss":"Mareshah, the name of two Israelites and of a place in P","kjv":"Mareshah","count":2,"share":0.22},{"strong":"H1245","lemma":"בָּקַשׁ","xlit":"bâqash","gloss":"to search out","kjv":"ask, beg, beseech, desire","count":3,"share":0.33}],"verses":["Josh.15.24","Josh.15.55","1Sam.23.14","1Sam.23.15","1Sam.23.24","1Sam.26.2","1Chr.2.42","1Chr.4.16","2Chr.11.8"],"related":[{"id":"deserts","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.035,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"maon","type":"lexical","strong":"H2128","why":"both lead with זִיף (H2128)"},{"id":"mareshah","type":"lexical","strong":"H2128","why":"both lead with זִיף (H2128)"},{"id":"desert","type":"lexical","strong":"H4057","why":"both lead with מִדְבָּר (H4057)"},{"id":"deserts","type":"lexical","strong":"H4057","why":"both lead with מִדְבָּר (H4057)"},{"